{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786056606201,"sessionID":"ses_026bcee0cffefRImV5o4n3VyGz","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_2711cf1e7dd54d708210dda4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"People judge how random a sequence is by reading it toss by toss and\ntracking how surprising each new outcome feels given the outcome that\ncame before it: in particular, they hold a mild expectation that outcomes\nwill alternate rather than repeat, so a long run of the same symbol\nrepeatedly violates that expectation and accumulates surprise. A sequence\nis judged more random when its total accumulated surprise over the run is\nclose to what a genuinely independent (fair-coin) run would produce, and\nless random when it accumulates too little surprise (a tightly forced,\nartificially even alternation) or too much (suspiciously long, repeating\nstreaks).\n","filePath":"/Users/ben/Documents/auto-psych/data/subjective_randomness/holdout_recovery_deepseek/holdout_runs/local_representativeness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_1/hypothesis.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/ben/Documents/auto-psych/data/subjective_randomness/holdout_recovery_deepseek/holdout_runs/local_representativeness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_1/hypothesis.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"data/subjective_randomness/holdout_recovery_deepseek/holdout_runs/local_representativeness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_1/hypothesis.md","time":{"start":1786056606175,"end":1786056606182}},"id":"prt_fd94500370014HByN4HIUCQrcr","sessionID":"ses_026bcee0cffefRImV5o4n3VyGz","messageID":"msg_fd944c1fd001PprTegXm2LdLc0"}}
